Change /output/lib/python/unicodedata.mjs — function isPrintable (line 50) and the UNPRINTABLE regex (line 10). Stop deriving printability from the host engine's Unicode tables and pin it to Unicode 15.0 (CPython 3.12's unidata_version).

Minimal patch I validated in a scratch copy (drops full-range divergence from 627 to 0):

  // Unicode 15.1 additions; unassigned (Cn) in Unicode 15.0, which CPython 3.12 ships.
  const ASSIGNED_AFTER_15_0 = [[0x2ffc, 0x2fff], [0x31ef, 0x31ef], [0x2ebf0, 0x2ee5d]];

  export function isPrintable(character) {
    if (character === ' ') return true;
    const cp = character.codePointAt(0);
    if (ASSIGNED_AFTER_15_0.some(([lo, hi]) => cp >= lo && cp <= hi)) return false;
    return !UNPRINTABLE.test(character);
  }

No change needed in /output/lib/python/repr.mjs — its escapeUnprintable already matches CPython byte for byte once isPrintable returns false.

Caveat: the above is a patch against today's ICU, not a true pin. A future ICU/Node bump (Unicode 16.0 adds further code points) will silently reintroduce the same class of mismatch. The durable fix is to ship a generated Unicode 15.0 C/Z range table in unicodedata.mjs and stop consulting \p{C}/\p{Z} entirely. (isDecimalDigit/decimalValue currently have no skew but share the same fragility and should be pinned in the same pass.)

Change the argv acquisition in /output/test14.mjs (line 48). Replace

  const args = parser.parse_args(process.argv.slice(2));

with argv recovered from the real process bytes and decoded with PEP 383 surrogateescape, e.g. a new helper module (/output/lib/python/argvbytes.mjs) exporting rawArgs():

  - read /proc/self/cmdline as a Buffer, split on NUL into fields;
  - take the LAST (process.argv.length - 2) fields (taking the tail, rather than dropping the first two, keeps it robust to `node` flags preceding the script path);
  - decode each field as UTF-8, and on any invalid byte b emit String.fromCharCode(0xDC00 + b) and advance one byte. Treat as invalid: continuation/0xC0/0xC1/0xF5+ lead bytes, truncated sequences, non-continuation bytes mid-sequence, overlong encodings (3-byte cp < 0x800, 4-byte cp < 0x10000), encoded surrogates (0xD800..0xDFFF) and cp > 0x10FFFF;
  - fall back to process.argv.slice(2) if /proc is unreadable (non-Linux) or the field count is short.

Then call parser.parse_args(rawArgs()).

Do NOT change /output/lib/python/repr.mjs — reprString already renders lone surrogates exactly as CPython does ('\udcc3(') and truncateRepr already counts code points, so once the argv string carries the surrogates the message, the code-point count and the 200-char %.200R truncation boundary all match automatically.

For the reported repro command, stderr line 7 should read:
  ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: '\udcc3('

